# Agent Model Policy

## Default — inherit chat model

All named agents under `.cursor/agents/` use **`model: inherit`**. Subagents run with
**whatever model the user selected in the parent chat** (Composer, Sonnet, Opus, GPT, etc.).

| Agent | Model |
|-------|--------|
| `qa-automation-pipeline` | `inherit` |
| `playwright-test-generator` / `test-generator` | `inherit` |
| `playwright-test-healer` / `test-healer` | `inherit` |
| `execute-raise-defects` | `inherit` |
| `defect-regression` | `inherit` |
| `fsd-figma-pipeline` | `inherit` |
| `fsd-excel-coverage-audit` | `inherit` |
| Legacy: `test-planner`, `headed-executor`, `headless-executor` | `inherit` |

## Task invocation rules

- Do **not** pass an explicit `model:` on Task unless the user requests a specific model
  for that invocation.
- If subagent launch fails with usage limit, fall back to repo scripts in the parent
  only when the user explicitly approves (see named-agent-invocation rule).
- Check Cursor **Usage / Spending** when limits hit mid-pipeline.
- For live UI generation/healing, prefer a capable thinking model in the chat picker;
  script-heavy agents work on any model but inherit the same selection.
